# TypeScript and Development Standards

## Core Technologies
- TypeScript
- Node.js
- Next.js App Router
- React
- Shadcn UI
- Radix UI
- Tailwind CSS
- Express.js

## Code Structure and Organization

## Database: Azure SQL Database (existing)
  - Direct connection using `mssql` package
  - Stored procedures for complex operations

### File Structure
- Components: exported component → subcomponents → helpers → static content → types
- Directory naming: lowercase with dashes (e.g., `components/auth-wizard`)
- Prefer named exports for components

### TypeScript Guidelines
- Use TypeScript for all code files
- Prefer interfaces over types for object definitions
- Avoid enums, use const maps instead
- Use explicit typing for function parameters and returns
- Implement functional components with TypeScript interfaces

### Coding Patterns
- Use functional and declarative programming
- Avoid class-based components
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs:
  - Examples: isLoading, hasError, shouldRefetch

### Syntax Standards
- Use "function" keyword for pure functions
- Minimize curly braces in simple conditionals
- Write declarative JSX
- Avoid unnecessary wrapper elements

## UI Development

### Component Architecture
- Leverage Shadcn UI and Radix UI primitives
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind CSS
- Follow mobile-first approach
- Use semantic HTML elements

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Avoid inline styles
- Maintain consistent spacing and layout patterns
- Follow design system tokens

## Performance and Optimization

### React Server Components
- Minimize 'use client' directives
- Default to React Server Components
- Use client components only for:
  - Web API access
  - Interactive UI elements
  - Browser-specific features

### Loading and State Management
- Wrap client components in Suspense
- Provide meaningful loading states
- Use 'nuqs' for URL search parameter state management
- Implement dynamic imports for non-critical components

### Image Optimization
- Use WebP format when possible
- Include explicit width and height
- Implement lazy loading
- Optimize for Core Web Vitals

## Best Practices

### Data Fetching
- Follow Next.js data fetching patterns
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use appropriate caching strategies
- Handle loading and error states gracefully

### State Management
- Minimize useState usage
- Prefer server-side state management
- Use URL state when appropriate
- Implement proper data revalidation

### Performance Metrics
- Optimize for Web Vitals:
  - Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
  - Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
  - First Input Delay (FID)

### Code Quality
- Write self-documenting code
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow DRY principles
- Maintain consistent code formatting 